  "native_text": "intentionally trigger catastrophic defaults with Damerau's construction lenders and insurers.1 \nManufactured Paralysis: The Six Impossible Preconditions \nTo maintain the immense leverage required to force the $8 million buyout, Giacovas had to \nensure the underlying HVAC dispute remained permanently deadlocked.1 If the HVAC unit were \nsuccessfully relocated, the injunction would dissolve, evaporating the extortionate leverage.1 \nIn a documented email dated June 3, 2024, Giacovas outlined six rigid, impossible \n\"preconditions\" that the Board had to flawlessly execute before he would \"even consider\" \nallowing the temporary relocation of the equipment.1 \nPrecondition Demanded by Giacovas \nStrategic Coercive Purpose \n1. Complete Engineer's Structural Report \nDesigned to force the majority owner to \nincur massive, punitive upfront engineering \ncosts before relocation viability was even \nassessed. \n2. Comprehensive Relocation Placement \nPlan \nDemanded while Giacovas simultaneously \nand aggressively denied Damerau's \ncontractors physical access to Unit 1 to \ngenerate the plan. \n3. Exact Project Timeline \nDemanded to create inflexible legal \ndeadlines that could later be leveraged for \nbreach of contract or contempt motions. \n4. Interim Cooling Solution \nIntended to shift the entire operational \nburden of Unit 1's habitability onto the \ndeveloper, exponentially increasing the \nfinancial \"burn rate\" of the delayed project. \n5. Contractor Cost Estimates \nUtilized purely as an intelligence-gathering \nmechanism to probe Damerau's financial \nbacking and calibrate the $8 million \nextortion demand. \n6. Total Indemnification Agreement \nForced the developer to assume 100% of \nthe financial risk for moving an aging, \n",
